09/2019: FP realizes that several changes from CODE2 to CODE3 were incorrect, which is temporary called CODE3fixed. This includes:

- MAJOR CHANGES IN CODE3
• adding halo cell and incorrect updated for fd1 and fd2 in higrad.f (WRONG any time because of
   the size of these array np+1,mp,l and not required)
• incorrect use of a tmp=0 file for BC of f1avg in force.f (WRONG with cyclic BC)
• I moved back to the optimization in firetec.f available in CODE2 (fuel stuff are computed only when
  fuel is present). Otherwise just gas phase on large time step. Detailed tests showed that this optimisation is correct. The only reason why it could give slightly different result from the none optimized version is because in fortran it is not equivalent to do : u = u+f*dt and do i=1:10 u=u+f*dts
• There is a flag impdataold in gridlist to know if we want the new version of mpdata, which is clean but potentially wrong in case of topo, and the old mpdata (which was called by Jon Reisner mpdata_new3d and which has been renamed as mpdataold for clarity)
• We included in gridlist a parameter call igniteVerticalExtend is order to set in which cells we want the ignition (if 0, the ignition is done in all cells, but if it is for example 3 or 5, ignition is only proceeded for k<=3 or 5...)
• We removed the interruption of reaction during ignition in firetec.f, which was incorrect in most cases especially when multiple ignition at different times occur

